This entry shows the multi-line form:
the header above carries the date and tag and stays on one line,
while these continuation lines use semantic breaks.

A blank line starts a new paragraph, one idea each.
agenda ignores this entry entirely (:reference:),
so it is structured purely for reading later.

***                                   ***                                    ***

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-07-02 Thu | Renewed the domain in time :todo: :done: completed:2026-07-02
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

***                                   ***                                    ***

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-07-05 Sun | Repaint the fence :todo: threshold:2026-09-01
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Not worth starting before autumn -- paint won't cure right in summer heat.
Hidden from agenda until the threshold date; then it behaves like any
other open :todo:.

***                                   ***                                    ***

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-07-08 Wed | Paid the property tax :todo: completed:2026-07-08
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No :done: tag here -- completed: alone is enough to exclude this line
from every section; the date itself is evidence the item is finished.

